<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="description" content="Northline Journal — notes on cities, objects and everyday culture.">
  <title>Northline Journal</title>
  <style>
    :root{color-scheme:light;--ink:#18211c;--paper:#f5f1e8;--line:#c8c1b2;--accent:#b94b32}
    *{box-sizing:border-box}html{scroll-behavior:smooth}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:16px/1.6 Georgia,"Times New Roman",serif}
    a{color:inherit;text-decoration:none}a:hover{color:var(--accent)}header,main,footer{width:min(1120px,calc(100% - 40px));margin:auto}
    header{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:28px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .brand{font:700 1rem/1 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase}.issue{font:13px/1 Arial,sans-serif;color:#62685f}
    .lead{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.45fr .75fr;gap:56px;padding:80px 0 72px}.kicker{font:700 12px/1 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent)}
    h1{max-width:780px;margin:18px 0 24px;font-size:clamp(3.2rem,8vw,7.3rem);font-weight:400;line-height:.92;letter-spacing:-.055em}
    .intro{max-width:620px;margin:0;font-size:1.22rem;color:#465048}.aside{align-self:end;border-top:1px solid var(--ink);padding-top:18px}
    .aside p{margin:0 0 20px}.date{font:12px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d716c}
    .stories{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);border-top:1px solid var(--ink);border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink)}
    article{min-height:280px;padding:34px 28px 42px;border-right:1px solid var(--line)}article:last-child{border-right:0}
    .number{font:12px/1 Arial,sans-serif;color:var(--accent)}h2{margin:52px 0 15px;font-size:1.7rem;line-height:1.12;font-weight:400}
    article p{margin:0;color:#596159}.note{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:36px;padding:56px 0}.note h3{margin:0;font:700 13px/1.2 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.13em;text-transform:uppercase}
    .note p{max-width:680px;margin:0;color:#4f5750}footer{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:24px 0 42px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);font:12px/1.4 Arial,sans-serif;color:#73776f}
    @media(max-width:760px){.lead{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:42px;padding:54px 0}.stories{grid-template-columns:1fr}article{min-height:auto;border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}article:last-child{border-bottom:0}.note{display:block}.note p{margin-top:22px}footer{display:block}footer span{display:block;margin-top:8px}}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header><a class="brand" href="/">Northline Journal</a><span class="issue">Issue 07 · Autumn</span></header>
  <main>
    <section class="lead">
      <div><div class="kicker">Field notes</div><h1>Small observations, carefully kept.</h1><p class="intro">An independent notebook about useful objects, changing streets and the quiet decisions that shape everyday life.</p></div>
      <aside class="aside"><p>We publish slowly: one considered collection at a time, without feeds, trends or notifications.</p><span class="date">Edited in Northern Europe</span></aside>
    </section>
    <section class="stories">
      <article><span class="number">01</span><h2>The last repair shop on the block</h2><p>A morning with the people who keep old tools, radios and kitchen clocks in use.</p></article>
      <article><span class="number">02</span><h2>Notes from a rainy platform</h2><p>What railway stations reveal when the timetable slows down and everyone has to wait.</p></article>
      <article><span class="number">03</span><h2>A chair designed to be forgotten</h2><p>On ordinary furniture, honest materials and the value of things that do their job quietly.</p></article>
    </section>
    <section class="note"><h3>About the journal</h3><p>Northline is a small editorial project maintained by a loose group of writers and photographers. New editions appear when the work is ready.</p></section>
  </main>
  <footer><span>© 2026 Northline Journal</span><span>__DOMAIN__</span></footer>
</body>
</html>
